---
/**
 * "Three organizations share the Village Green name."
 *
 * This is the single easiest thing for a visitor — or a grant reviewer — to
 * get wrong, and the board is acutely aware of it. In mock-up 2 it was quiet
 * footer text. Betsy asked for the prominence it had in mock-up 3: its own
 * bordered card, with a heading, in the flow of the page. That is decision 010,
 * and it is the one element carried across from a retired mock-up.
 *
 * The wording is checked against docs/organization.md. Do not paraphrase it
 * without reading that file — the distinction between owning the land, owning
 * the building, and supporting the programs is legally and politically real.
 */
---

<aside class="disambiguation" aria-labelledby="disambiguation-heading">
  <h2 id="disambiguation-heading">Three organizations share the Village Green name</h2>

  {/* Keep each <b> on the same line as the word before it. A line break
      directly before a tag is collapsed away, which silently glues the words
      together — "The<b>Village Green Foundation</b>". */}
  <p>
    The <b>Metropolitan Park District</b> owns the land.
    The <b>Village Green Foundation</b> owns the building.
    We are <b>Friends of the Village Green</b>, an all-volunteer group that
    supports some of the programs and the people who run them. We do not run
    the Community Center.
  </p>
</aside>

<style>
  .disambiguation {
    max-width: var(--width-prose);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-accent);
    padding: var(--space-l);
    background: var(--color-bg-alt);
  }

  /* Smaller than a section heading — this is an aside, not a chapter. The
     element is still an h2 so the document outline stays correct. */
  .disambiguation h2 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: 0;
  }

  .disambiguation p {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-top: var(--space-s);
  }

  .disambiguation b {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
